			"details": "Library for encoding/decoding names. An ENS name is stop-separated labels, eg. \"aaa.bb.c\". A DNS-encoded name is composed of byte length-prefixed labels with a terminator byte. eg. \"\\x03aaa\\x02bb\\x01c\\x00\". * maximum label length is 255 bytes. * length = 0 is reserved for the terminator (root). * `dns.length == 2 + ens.length` and the mapping is injective.",
